add('<p>In Arbitrage Pricing Theory, alpha is the intercept left after compensation for the specified factor exposures, so it is model-dependent. My opinion: FUND2 is the only plausible candidate for an alpha fee, conditional on fees, costs, and out-of-sample validation. Its FF3 alpha remains positive with a t statistic above two, while the four-factor model adds little for FUND2 by AICc; for FUND1 the four-factor model is clearly preferred and its alpha disappears. The realized five-year returns differ from projections based on a different ten-year factor window. This makes factor-based expected returns useful scenarios, but fragile single inputs for an optimizer, especially with uncertain premia and betas.</p>')
